  "description": "A magnetic field sensor in two parts, in series on your supply. The current enters the Hall bar's left end (its carriers are positive), leaves its right end into the junction, and crosses a short, wide strip of the electron metal to ground; that strip resists more as the field grows, whichever way the field points. Make a current between 2.1 and 2.9 flow through the wide strip, the junction sit between 3.6 and 4.5, and the Hall bar's top contact sit 3 to 8 above its bottom one (averaged over $t = 10$ to $80$). The wide strip reads the field's strength but not its sign; the Hall bar reads its sign.",
